# Activity 1: Promotional Event Poster Design ("Free Coffee")

## Description
This activity involved designing a promotional event poster for **Arrupe Hall Booth 7** scheduled for **Tuesday, August 4, 2026**[cite: 2]. The poster advertises a free coffee giveaway using bold, stacked display typography layered with an iced coffee splash visual and warm earth-toned colors to attract student attention[cite: 2].

## What Have I Learned?
- **Key Concepts & Skills:** I learned how to use visual hierarchy, typography, and focal point placement to communicate key event details (date, location, and call to action) at a single glance[cite: 2].
- **Challenge & Solution:** One challenge I faced was layering the central coffee splash graphic with the repeated "FREE COFFEE" text without sacrificing readability; I solved this by adjusting element sizing, contrast, and spacing so the text remained legible around the focal image[cite: 2].
- **Future Application & Improvement:** I can apply these layout principles when creating health awareness posters or campus event announcements in the future, and I could improve this design by adding subtle scheduling hours or a QR code for event registration.
